<speak version="1.0" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis" xml:lang="en-US">
  <voice name="en-US-AndrewNeural" id="seg1"><prosody rate="+5%">Broadcasters want AI commentary. But a fluent sentence can still be wrong, and live, there's no undo. So before any model gets the mic, it has to pass this test.<break time="400ms"/></prosody></voice>
  <voice name="en-US-AndrewNeural" id="seg2"><prosody rate="+5%">Six narrators call the same seeded matches, each with planted traps: a red card, a stoppage-time penalty, a late winner. One fixed referee scores every claim. <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ɡrɑk">Grok</phoneme> four point seven tops the table, but takes seventy seconds a claim. <say-as interpret-as="characters">GPT</say-as> four point one fell for none of the fourteen traps, in under three seconds. That's the live pick. <say-as interpret-as="characters">GPT</say-as> five <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈnænoʊ">nano</phoneme> fell for eight. Not cleared.<break time="400ms"/></prosody></voice>
  <voice name="en-US-AndrewNeural" id="seg3"><prosody rate="+5%">Click any narrator to see its worst moment beside the others. Same frame, same facts. Here, five narrators named the right scorer. But <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈnænoʊ">nano</phoneme> couldn't point to the fact that names him, so it never aired. True isn't enough. It has to be provable.<break time="400ms"/> And when the referee fixes wording, you see exactly what changed.</prosody></voice>
  <voice name="en-US-AndrewNeural" id="seg4"><prosody rate="+5%">Then deploy. Use on Desk puts a cleared narrator on a live match. <say-as interpret-as="characters">GPT</say-as> four point one narrates, and every claim shows checking, then stands, amended or overturned, with the evidence on the pitch. Nothing goes on air until it survives review.</prosody></voice>
  <voice name="en-US-AndrewNeural" id="seg5"><prosody rate="+5%">The narrator is replaceable. The exam and the referee are the asset. That's <sub alias="Match proof">Matchproof</sub>.<break time="400ms"/> Built on Microsoft Foundry, Agent Framework and Azure. Rig the match. Catch the narrator.</prosody></voice>
</speak>
